            "subject": "LU-20730 llapi: read a namespace walk as LFU chunks"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Artem Blagodarenko",
          "email": "ablagodarenko@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-04 15:06:28.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Artem Blagodarenko",
          "email": "ablagodarenko@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-04 21:01:44.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20730 llapi: run find over a device's LFU chunks",
        "message": "LU-20730 llapi: run find over a device's LFU chunks\n\nllapi_find_device() takes its records one callback at a time from\nllapi_scan_device(), so lfs find --device does not exercise the LFU\nObject Stream at all.\n\nRead the target through llapi_lfu_open() instead, 64 slots of 64 KiB\na read, and judge each record with the same find_device_cb(). Add\nscan_device_lfu_rec(), which puts a chunk's LfuInode and raw EAs back\ninto the object a backend hands over and builds the record with\nscan_rec_build(), split out of scan_sink_object(), so both paths read\nthe bytes alike. The FID is the producer's. Without the linkea, which\nis sent only when the search needs it, the class is the target's own\nsubject matter, as only that is sent by default.\n\nThe stream has no field for the object's id on the target, so a\nsearch that needs it, -printf %i or LLAPI_SCAN_F_INTERNAL with its\nFID-less objects, still reads records. printf_format_want() now\nreports %i as LLAPI_SCAN_INO to tell. An object whose LMA names no\nvalid FID is not sent, and so not printed, on the chunk path; the\nsearch warns how many there were, from the chunks' error count.\n\nconf-sanity 300a compares lfs find --device -printf '%LF' (chunks)\nwith -printf '%LF %i' (records); it fails with a decoder that flips\none FID bit and passes with this patch. conf-sanity 300a-300d pass.\nOn a 100k-file MDT the search takes 0.45 s over chunks against 0.43 s\nover records.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTest-Parameters: testlist=conf-sanity env=ONLY=300a,300b,300c,300d\nSigned-off-by: Artem Blagodarenko <ablagodarenko@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: I10c6ab74f447babea827294136a1dfab6e759e0e\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
